  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_5152bafa77104506bbbde55d08cac344",
      "statement": "A callback spec is a `@dataclass` whose dataclass fields are the knob allow-list enforced by `CallbackRegistry.resolve` (an unknown knob raises `ValueError` before any callback is built), and `CallbackRegistry.register` refuses a non-dataclass with `TypeError`; specs satisfy the `CallbackSpec` Protocol structurally through a `build(ctx) -> pl.Callback` method and may declare optional class-level `logged_metrics` / `monitor_metric` attributes that `validate_monitor` reads defensively via `getattr`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/registry.py#L140-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77bf50475e6b912150fa3e11b2b27e6cac89c995a66d530c1006df53e85c72a8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/registry.py#L30-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6c329e327e1ffa524fcfccc10f6074664e7b06bfbd787b23e0efb83db17232a1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/registry.py#L99-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09a7d1a91cd4c707609f1743770a74881deb61a7243aec7f6e311d1f5706b8a9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_106406cda18b4a3f9149c7fae4227ed7",
      "statement": "Callback construction is two-phase: `CallbackRegistry.resolve(names, cfg)` validates names (unknown name -> `KeyError` listing the registered set) and per-name knob dicts (unknown knob -> `ValueError` listing the allowed fields) at config time and returns dataclass spec instances in `names` order with unsupplied fields taking their defaults, while `CallbackRegistry.build(specs, ctx)` injects the runtime `CallbackContext` at fit-prep and returns the constructed `pl.Callback` list; the split exists because generative callbacks need runtime objects that do not exist at config resolution.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adr/0029-callback-registry.md#L7-L13",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:659edceaf88dca75f7e7b63af89f619fa3b1381b27d5db3fdd787ea50edc2c88:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/registry.py#L73-L112",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3d7771a57cea33ba534cb829e7c7670a61e39a7a9d581c893f0fc2a14e6f8289:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0d50c70258804c78be630f5b715989f4",
      "statement": "`CallbackContext` is a frozen dataclass runtime-objects bag carrying `module`, `vae`, `datamodule`, `inference_recipe`, `model_dir` and `seed` plus the optional `feature_net`, `feature_net_factory` and `real_latents`; all fields are `Any`-typed so the callbacks package stays free of import cycles back into the module / data / metrics layers, and a spec's `build` casts as needed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/context.py#L17-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:68e4dc667f042163c1906b0d695116ed3cde6e50aa3edcee67c45fee3f78bf69:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7707634286b042d385245ab1489345af",
      "statement": "`CallbackRegistry.validate_monitor` runs after resolve/build and before the trainer is built: it picks the first resolved spec carrying a `monitor_metric` attribute, treats `monitor_metric=None` (or no checkpoint spec) as the intended unmonitored fallback and returns without checking, and otherwise requires the metric to appear in the union of every spec's `logged_metrics`, the training module's `logged_metrics`, and every `extra_callbacks` member's `logged_metrics`, raising `ValueError` with the available set when nobody logs it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/registry.py#L114-L154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:af95f5276d1be7a22b7e75a5b7011bdbe4161b0dcf37dda3ba850149d5855b7e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f4f8a5cc29344aad98731e7695f380a7",
      "statement": "Four specs are exported from the callbacks barrel: `TrainLossSpec` (no knobs -> `TrainLossLogger`, logs `train/loss_epoch`), `FIDSpec` (`num_synth=16`, `every_n_epochs=1`, `center_slices_ratio=0.5`, `cov_ridge=1e-6` -> `FIDCallback`, logs `val/fid`), `CheckpointSpec` (`monitor_metric`, `save_top_k=3`, `save_last`, `every_n_epochs`, `mode`, `filename` -> `pl.callbacks.ModelCheckpoint`), and `PairedFidelitySpec` (`subset_size=8`, `every_n_epochs=1`, `num_inference_steps=None`, `seed=0` -> `PairedFidelityCallback`, logs `val/psnr` / `val/ssim`); each declares `logged_metrics` as a `ClassVar` so it stays out of the knob allow-list.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/__init__.py#L14-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64c3a8aa31289e593919d410a09dc2addd0f8f51e1caead5b1efb9e3c6369453:"
