    {
      "id": "claim_bfe0ab867e454caeb90cf66a6b4b2b14",
      "statement": "`PairedFidelitySpec.build` is recipe-primary: when its `num_inference_steps` knob is `None` it reads `ctx.inference_recipe[\"num_inference_steps\"]` and falls back to the literal 15, while an explicit per-callback knob overrides the recipe; the supervised ControlNet shell now fills the previously-`None` `CallbackContext.inference_recipe` with `{\"num_inference_steps\": ...}` sourced from the existing `controlnet.num_inference_steps` recipe knob (default 15, i.e. 29 UNet evals for the two-eval Heun rollout), so the step count lives in one place.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adr/0037-controlnet-fidelity-in-training-monitor.md#L49-L56",
