    {
      "id": "claim_eae248d505ed4af7924aa96e424e07b7",
      "statement": "`TrainingSpine.run` is the single registry caller and applies a fixed merge order: the shell's `default_names` are replaced wholesale by `callback_names_override` (the CLI `--callbacks` flag), `forbidden_callbacks` then force-removes named callbacks post-merge with a `rank_zero_info` log so no YAML knob or CLI override can re-enable them, `forbidden_monitors` raises `ValueError` on a forbidden `callback_cfg[\"checkpoint\"][\"monitor_metric\"]` before resolution, and only then are specs resolved, built, extended with `extra_callbacks`, and monitor-validated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/core.py#L108-L151",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:94c3b227a0fb72682eb80a4db6c34bb0a9d496d6b0209c7995ec048c0fee86ed:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_eb3f6ae4821542219b9ecfc875ec3134",
      "statement": "If no `ModelCheckpoint` survives the merge, `TrainingSpine.run` raises a `ValueError` whose message names the resolved callback list and demands a `'checkpoint'` entry, instead of letting `next(...)` raise `StopIteration` deeper in the call (codex #170 P2).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/core.py#L141-L151",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bef2e4037c4ac5cd3263067f9cb3ad3b0ddabd53facc2500ffb73e853370a886:"
        },
        {
