    {
      "id": "claim_c2ec4b1b48664d2289b824bb07492dce",
      "statement": "`tests/test_callback_registry.py` is the focused test module for the registry and spine, covering fail-fast resolve on an unknown name and an unknown knob, the build phase for the train-loss / FID / checkpoint specs, the six `validate_monitor` paths (callback-logged, unlogged, module-declared, `monitor_metric=None`, extra-callback-logged, extra-callback-absent), six `PairedFidelitySpec` cases including the recipe-primary step count, the missing-`ModelCheckpoint` fail-fast, and the two forbidden-policy guards; the minimal validation command is `pytest tests/test_callback_registry.py -q`.",
