    {
      "id": "claim_42741e6e6d2f4a5d9430db6a887865fe",
      "statement": "Extending the paired-fidelity monitor to the ControlNet-GRPO path is deliberately still open: it would require releasing the GRPO shell's blanket `forbidden_callbacks={\"fid\": ...}` for this callback specifically (its rollout uses the ControlNet, unlike unconditional FID) and keeping the VAE on GPU for the decode — a separate follow-up per ADR-0037, not part of the supervised-stage change.",
